cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "SoulBench SNAP v3.1: a preliminary audit of prompt-conditioned response profiles in six language models"
abstract: >-
  Code, configuration, data and manuscript of SNAP v3.1, a compact pilot that
  collected 2,700 single-turn responses from six language-model endpoints
  (15 items, three system conditions, ten scheduled runs), coded them with two
  LLM judges and tested pre-set stability and context-robustness criteria. The
  pipeline completed; the scientific decision is FAIL.
type: software
authors:
